    road 2, along 0.2°N: 0.5°E – 0.9°E (barrier=border_control) – 1.1°E – 1.5°E                at a checkpoint
    road 3, along 0.3°N: 0.5°E – 0.99°E (barrier) – 1.1°E – 1.5°E – 1.9°E (barrier) – 2.1°E – 2.5°E
                         across AAA, BBB and CCC, and a spur from 1.5°E north to 0.35°N, so 1.5°E is a junction
    road 4, along 0.4°N: 0.5°E – 0.1°E – 0.1°W – 0.5°W                 leaves AAA for no zone at 0°, no barrier

  Each edge across a border is the one segment that crosses it, so a checkpoint at its end is on it. A table
  crossing at (0.1°N, 1°E) is on road 1 and 11 km from road 2.

  0.1° of longitude is 11.12 km here, 667 s at the wheel and 0.2224 h of travel. In whole seconds at the wheel:

